+# Anonymous expert review template — draft v1
+
+Case ID: __________  Reviewer code: __________  Date: __________
+
+Review the anonymous proposals and common evidence packet. Method, model, generation stage, and analyst mapping are not provided. Record possible unblinding if a passage reveals identity or stage.
+
+## Per-proposal ratings
+
+Use 1–5: 1 = major defects; 2 = substantial weaknesses; 3 = plausible but incomplete; 4 = strong with limited weaknesses; 5 = unusually strong for this question. Rate scientific content rather than writing style. Distinguish explicitly labeled assumptions from unsupported claims presented as established facts.
+
+| Proposal ID | Evidence grounding | Causal rigor | Specificity | Testability | Feasibility | Optional novelty |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| | | | | | | |
+| | | | | | | |
+| | | | | | | |
+| | | | | | | |
+| | | | | | | |
+
+For each proposal record its main strength, consequential weakness or factual error with source ID, unsupported assumption most likely to invalidate it, and whether its proposed observation distinguishes the stated alternatives. Record important points outside your expertise. Novelty is descriptive; unfamiliarity does not establish originality.
+
+## Overall pair preference
+
+Choose the scientifically stronger and more useful proposal considering the five main dimensions. Select a tie when no preference is defensible. Anonymous pairs are supplied by the export tool after generation.
+
+| Pair ID | Left proposal | Right proposal | Prefer left / tie / prefer right | Reason and critical caveat |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| | | | | |
+
+Primary analysis compares final multi-model and final single-model proposals separately for ALS and AML. Initial-to-final comparisons are secondary. Two problems with one run each do not establish general superiority. Retain individual expert ratings and disagreements.
+
+Possible unblinding: __________
+Source or expertise limitations: __________
+Additional verification needed: __________
